    {
      "title": null,
      "text": "%md\n## Getting the files to the project\nWhile `SAVE_TO_FOLDER = False`, the extracts live only in this Spark session (tables named like\n`bt_2026_03_31`); you can query them in new paragraphs, but they are gone when the session stops.\nOnce you have a folder you can write to, set `SAVE_TO_FOLDER = True` and re-run paragraphs 4 and 5.\nEach extract is then a **folder** in `OUT_DIR` holding one CSV named `part-....csv`.\nIn Hue's file browser, open each folder, download the CSV, and save it in the project as:\n\n* main extracts: `data\\\\bt_<date>.csv` and `data\\\\live_2026-09-30.csv`\n* Track B: `data\\\\trackb\\\\trackb_<name>.csv`\n\nThen, in Git Bash: `python main.py check \"data/*.csv\"`",
